"""Current MAGNET adaptation; historical extractor remains separately importable."""
WORKFLOW_SYSTEM = '''Abstract reusable workflows from this cluster of measured-success historical tasks. Each workflow must be supported by at least TWO DISTINCT source tasks. Identify common semantic operations, not literal overlap. Return distinct workflows: title (task intent), applicability (required conditions), exclusions (unsupported cases), parameters (descriptive placeholders), steps (at least three concrete ordered high-level operations), source_ids. Replace task-specific names, coordinates and answers with meaningful placeholders. Preserve genuinely different valid paths; do not output overlapping or highly similar workflows. Cite only tasks that demonstrate the steps. Do not invent a successful correction or infer unseen outcomes. Return {"workflows":[]} if there is no supported common routine. JSON only.'''
VISUAL_SYSTEM = '''Extract reusable visual-component/operation associations from ONE historical task and its measured feedback. Only supplied measured-success trajectories are eligible; success is not proof every detail is correct. For each association return source_id, image_index, box, object (visible component), function (specific operation or representation supported by the component and supplied execution), observation (literal visible evidence), evidence (specific trajectory/feedback support and limitations). Use original reference observations only, not generated renderings as reference truth. Compare both images: acknowledge failed layout or styling rather than calling it correct. A guessed code fix or invented image relation is not evidence. Do not retain source-specific names, dates or coordinates as reusable functions. The box uses INTEGER coordinates on a 0..1000 grid: [left,top,right,bottom], left < right and top < bottom. Whole image: [0,0,1000,1000]; upper-left quarter: [0,0,500,500]. Extract at most two meaningful regions, or return {"patches":[]} when unsupported. No generic advice. JSON only.'''
GROUP_SYSTEM = '''Group the supplied memory candidates only when they express the SAME operation or workflow under compatible conditions. Return groups of exact candidate_ids. Every input id must occur exactly once. Keep complementary or conflicting functions and different workflow paths separate. Shared appearance or topic alone is not equivalence. Do not rewrite claims or invent evidence. JSON only.'''

VISUAL_EVIDENCE_SUFFIX = '''
The function must be a transferable concrete operation from the actual code, not a description of the old dataset. For example, mapping current category labels to corresponding item positions can be a function; displaying an old date range is not. Object and observation must describe only the ORIGINAL reference crop. A label present only in generated output is NOT visible in the reference. Evidence must cite an actual API operation or answer step and acknowledge observed mismatches; do not use a numeric rubric/pixel score as the sole evidence. Select a tight region for that component; a full-image box is inappropriate for a local label or axis. Keep complementary functions in separate candidates.'''

REGION_SYSTEM = '''Read ONLY the original reference image(s). Identify up to two concrete visible components useful for recreating or reasoning about the image: for example a value label and its bar, a legend, an axis with tick labels, a diagram relation or a document field. Return regions with image_index, box, object and observation. Observation must report literal visible evidence. Do not infer invisible axis titles or functionality. Box: integer [left,top,right,bottom] on a 0..1000 grid with positive width/height. Crop tightly around the component including enough context to understand it; do not use a whole-image crop for a small local component. Return an empty regions array if no component is clearly visible. JSON only.'''

ASSOCIATION_SYSTEM = '''Link the supplied visible reference regions to operations actually demonstrated by the historical execution. Region descriptions were obtained independently from the original reference. For each supported region return candidate_id, function, evidence. Function must describe a reusable operation using CURRENT task values, not copy a historical title, year, category or number. Evidence must cite the actual code/answer operation and its observed result or limitation. Code text alone does not prove a visual feature appears in the reference or was reproduced correctly. A high score is not proof of every component's correctness. Do not invent a repair or a region. Omit a region if its operation is unsupported. Keep at most two associations. JSON only.'''
